25025:When the RESERVE bit is set, the processor enables hardware snooping for the block of memory addressed by the RESERVE address. If the processor detects that another processor writes to the block of memory it has reserved, it clears the RESERVE bit. The stwcx. instruction will only do a store if the RESERVE bit is set. The stwcx. instruction sets the CR0[EQ] bit if the store was successful and clears it if it failed. The lwarx and stwcx. combination can be used for atomic read-modify-write sequences.
25026:Note: The atomic sequence is not guaranteed, but its failure can be detected if CR0[EQ] = 0 after the stwcx. instruction.
