30631:On implementations that support a virtual address size of only n bits, n 80, rS[0 to 79- n] must be zeros. The high-order bits of rB[52-63] that correspond to SLB entries beyond the size of the SLB provided by the implementation must be zeros. If this instruction is executed in 32-bit mode, rB[0-31] must be zeros (i.e., the ESID must be in the range 0-15). This instruction cannot be used to invalidate an SLB. This is a supervisor-level instruction.
