2915: The remainder of the fixed-point instructions use the     result placed into the target register. In 64-bit mode,
2916: contents of the General Purpose Registers (GPRs) as       these bits are set by signed comparison of the result
2917: source operands, and place results into GPRs, into the    to zero. In 32-bit mode, these bits are set by signed
2918: Fixed-Point Exception Register (XER), and into Condi-     comparison of the low-order 32 bits of the result to
2919: tion Register fields. In addition, the Trap instructions  zero.
2920: test the contents of a GPR or XER bit, invoking the
2921: system trap handler if the result of the specified test   Unless otherwise noted and when appropriate, when
2922: is true.                                                  CR Field 0 and the XER are set they reflect the value
2923:                                                           placed into the target register.
