968: 
969: Programming Environments Manual PowerPC RISC Microprocessor Family
970: 
971: 2.1.3.1 Condition Register CR0 Field Definition
972: For all integer instructions, when the CR is set to reflect the result of the operation (that is, when Rc = 1), and for addic., andi., and andis., the first three bits of CR0 are set by an algebraic comparison of the result to zero; the fourth bit of CR0 is copied from XER[SO]. For integer instructions, CR bits [0-3] are set to reflect the result as a signed quantity.
973: The CR bits are interpreted as shown in Table 2-1. If any portion of the result is undefined, the value placed into the first three bits of CR0 is undefined. The stwcx. and stdcx. instructions also set the CR0 field.
974: 
975: Table 2-1. Bit Settings for CR0 Field of CR
976: 
977: CR0 Bit 0 1 2 3
978: 
979: Description Negative (LT)--This bit is set when the result is negative. Positive (GT)--This bit is set when the result is positive (and not zero). Zero (EQ)--This bit is set when the result is zero or when a stwcx. or stdcx. successfully completes. Summary overflow (SO)--This is a copy of the final state of XER[SO] at the completion of the instruction.
980: 
981: Note: If overflow occurs, CR0 may not reflect the true (infinitely precise) result. CR0 bits [0-2] are undefined if Rc = 1 for the mulhw, mulhwu, divw, and divwu instructions in 64-bit mode.
982: 
983: 2.1.3.2 Condition Register CR1 Field Definition
984: In all floating-point instructions when the CR is set to reflect the result of the operation (Rc=1), CR1 (bits [4-7] of the CR) is copied from bits [0-3] of the FPSCR and indicates the floating-point exception status. For more information about the FPSCR, see Section 2.1.4 Floating-Point Status and Control Register (FPSCR). The bit settings for the CR1 field are shown in Table 2-2.
985: 
986: Table 2-2. Bit Settings for CR1 Field of CR
987: 
988: CR1 Bit 4 5 6 7
989: 
990: Description
991: Floating-point exception summary (FX)--This is a copy of the final state of FPSCR[FX] at the completion of the instruction.
992: Floating-point enabled exception summary (FEX)--This is a copy of the final state of FPSCR[FEX] at the completion of the instruction.
993: Floating-point invalid operation exception summary (VX)--This is a copy of the final state of FPSCR[VX] at the completion of the instruction.
994: Floating-point overflow exception (OX)--This is a copy of the final state of FPSCR[OX] at the completion of the instruction.
