A’s mask matches Book I for all 4,096 pairs: each loop terminates after 1–64 visits, with no position visited twice. B also passed checks covering every SH/MB/ME combination at both widths.

One correction to the supplied settled wording: Book I does explicitly say the upper half is cleared in a scoped `rlwinm` programming note at lines 4195–4196. That note covers the listed non-wrapping uses; it does not establish the PEM’s unconditional rule.

