28977:If executing in the default 64-bit mode and rA contains the most negative 64-bit number (0x8000_0000_0000_0000), the result is the most negative number and, if OE = 1, OV is set. Similarly, if executing in 32-bit mode of a 64-bit implementation (or on a 32-bit implementation) and the low-order 32 bits of rA contains the most negative 32-bit number (0x8000_0000), then the low-order 32 bits of the result contain the most negative 32-bit number and, if OE = 1, OV is set.

codex
The final distinction is between insertion and AND: `rlwimi` preserves destination bits outside the mask, while `rlwnm` clears them. Both use the same wrapping-mask rule. Both proposed handlers pass the final destination value to `update_cr0`; verifying the helper itself would require source outside this review’s scope.

